ize of the largest t-intersecting families of k-multisets from {[n]}_{\\infty }${[n]}_{\\infty }$ using an operation which they call down-compression. In [12], Meagher and Purdy used the down-compression operation from [8] and a graph homomorphism to prove the further results and gave the structure of the families that attain the maximum size.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHilton-Milner theorem for k-multisets (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0012365X25004911)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; In the special case when , our result gives rise to an unbounded multiset version for Hilton-Milner theorem given by Meagher and Purdy. ... Meagher and Purdy defined the graph with vertex-set , and two vertices are adjacent if and only if the corresponding k-multisets are disjoint.\n\n# Hilton-Milner theorem for k-multisets\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel Jiaqi Liao ^{a}, Mengyu Cao ^{b}, Zequn Lv ^{a}, Mei Lu ^{a}\n\nShow more\n\nCite\n\nAdd to Mendeley\n\nShare\n\n10.1016/j.disc.2025.114883\n\nAccess through your organizationPurchase PDF\n\nMore actions\n\n  * Article preview\n  * Recommended articles\n\n## Abstract\n\nLet and . A k-multiset in {[n]}_{m} is a multiset of cardinality k, whose elements are integers from , and each element is allowed to have at most m repetitions. A family of k-multisets in {[n]}_{m} is said to be intersecting if every pair of k-multisets from the family have non-empty intersection. In this paper, we give the size and structure of the largest non-trivial intersecting family of k-multisets in {[n]}_{m} for . In the special case when , our result gives rise to an unbounded multiset version for Hilton-Milner theorem given by Meagher and Purdy. Furthermore, our main theorem unites the statements of the Hilton-Milner theorem for finite sets and unbounded multisets.\nShortly after that, Meagher and Purdy [15] obtained the t-intersecting version of th